author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "A pm surface reports provenance coverage over the real history corpus - a pm health check, a pm validate check, or an ops verb - so the inert condition becomes observable without writing code; The report distinguishes a dimension no harness declares from a dimension declared by some harness and never observed, using the descriptor coverage analyzer rather than only the model summarizer; A gate fails, or at minimum warns with a recorded threshold, when a declared dimension is inert across a bounded recent window, so a signal that stops working is caught rather than silently degrading; The gate is proved capable of failing by a negative control, following the pattern pm-b2hc4x established, so it cannot join the set of gates that are structurally unable to fail; The measurement is bounded and resumable over the history streams so it stays inside token and latency budgets at million-item scale"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: 96
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Live bounded repository history is evaluated by the provenance coverage instrument with inert, missing, and undeclared signal diagnostics."
actual_result: "Provenance coverage now consumes the bounded immutable event index, compares configured descriptors with observed/unavailable/legacy values, emits stable inert and undeclared warnings, and reports source, truncation, and cursor receipts."
